window.DOCS["6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2"]={"id":"6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2","summary":{"title_zh":"名古屋議定書合規委員會第五次會議工作報告","what":"這份文件是名古屋議定書合規委員會第五次會議（2026 年 5 月，蒙特婁）的工作報告，由委員會提交，回顧各締約方執行議定書的進度，並向締約方會議（名古屋議定書第六次會議）提出建議，供其審議是否作出決定。","points":["提醒尚未提交第一份國家報告的締約方，應於名古屋議定書第六次會議前盡快提交。","表達關切：仍有 26% 的締約方未指定主管機關、54% 未指定檢查點，且近半數締約方有資訊尚未公布於取得與利益分享資訊交換所。","請尚未建立法律、行政與政策措施及相關制度的締約方，盡速落實，並將現有資訊完整公布於取得與利益分享資訊交換所。","建議各締約方加強對原住民族與地方社區的支持，協助其制定社區議定書並參與利益分享流程。","建議締約方會議請大會在財務機制指引中，請全球環境基金及時提供資金，支持符合條件的締約方準備並提交第二份國家報告。"],"open":[]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2/p001.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3"},{"t":"Distr.: General 5 June 2026"},{"t":"Original: English"},{"t":"Compliance Committee under the                               Conference of the Parties to the Convention\nNagoya Protocol on Access and Benefit-sharing                on Biological Diversity serving as the\nFifth meeting                                                meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya\nMontreal, Canada, 27–29 May 2026                             Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources\nAgenda item 7                                                and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of\nAdoption of the report                                       Benefits Arising from Their Utilization","tb":1},{"t":"Sixth meeting Yerevan, 19–30 October 2026 Item 5 of the provisional agenda* Report of the Compliance Committee"},{"t":"Report of the Compliance Committee under the Nagoya Protocol on the work of its fifth meeting"},{"t":"I.    Introduction"},{"t":"Attendance"},{"t":"1.    The following members of the Compliance Committee under the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from their Utilization and observer from indigenous peoples and local communities were present for the fifth meeting of the Committee:"},{"t":"African States                                   Latin American and Caribbean States\n      El Khitma El Awad Mohammed                 Teresa Dolores Cruz Sardiñas\n      Betty Kauna Schröder                       José Alfredo Hernández Ugalde","tb":1},{"t":"Etim Okon William"},{"t":"Western European and other States Marcus Schroeder Asia-Pacific States"},{"t":"Katie Beckett"},{"t":"Won Seog Park"},{"t":"Mery Ciacci"},{"t":"Somaly Chan"},{"t":"Indigenous peoples and local communities Eastern European States"},{"t":"Viviana Elsa Figueroa Elzbieta Martyniuk"},{"t":"Peter Maňka"},{"t":"Sino Tohirzoda"},{"t":"Item 1"},{"t":"Opening of the meeting"},{"t":"2.   The meeting was opened by the outgoing Chair of the Compliance Committee under the Nagoya Protocol, Betty Kauna Schröder. In her opening remarks, Ms. Schröder noted that the * CBD/NP/MOP/6/1."}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3\n發行：一般\n2026年6月5日\n原文：英文","html":"<p>CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3<br />\n發行：一般<br />\n2026年6月5日<br />\n原文：英文</p>","en":[0,1,2]},{"md":"名古屋議定書下之\n取得與利益分享\n遵約委員會\n第五屆會議\n加拿大，蒙特婁，2026年5月27–29日\n議程項目 7\n報告之採納","html":"<p>名古屋議定書下之<br />\n取得與利益分享<br />\n遵約委員會<br />\n第五屆會議<br />\n加拿大，蒙特婁，2026年5月27–29日<br />\n議程項目 7<br />\n報告之採納</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"生物多樣性公約締約方大會\n兼\n遺傳資源取得與其利用所產生利益之公平公正分享\n名古屋議定書締約方會議\n第六屆會議\n葉里溫，2026年10月19–30日\n臨時議程項目 5*\n遵約委員會報告","html":"<p>生物多樣性公約締約方大會<br />\n兼<br />\n遺傳資源取得與其利用所產生利益之公平公正分享<br />\n名古屋議定書締約方會議<br />\n第六屆會議<br />\n葉里溫，2026年10月19–30日<br />\n臨時議程項目 5*<br />\n遵約委員會報告</p>","en":[4,5]},{"md":"名古屋議定書下之遵約委員會第五屆會議工作報告","html":"<p>名古屋議定書下之遵約委員會第五屆會議工作報告</p>","en":[6,7]},{"md":"I. 前言","html":"<p>I. 前言</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"出席人員\n1. 以下為遺傳資源取得與其利用所產生利益之公平公正分享名古屋議定書下之遵約委員會成員，以及來自原住民族與地方社區之觀察員，出席委員會第五屆會議：","html":"<p>出席人員<br />\n1. 以下為遺傳資源取得與其利用所產生利益之公平公正分享名古屋議定書下之遵約委員會成員，以及來自原住民族與地方社區之觀察員，出席委員會第五屆會議：</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"非洲國家\nEl Khitma El Awad Mohammed\nBetty Kauna Schröder\nEtim Okon William","html":"<p>非洲國家<br />\nEl Khitma El Awad Mohammed<br />\nBetty Kauna Schröder<br />\nEtim Okon William</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"亞太國家\nWon Seog Park\nSomaly Chan","html":"<p>亞太國家<br />\nWon Seog Park<br />\nSomaly Chan</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"東歐國家\nElzbieta Martyniuk\nPeter Maňka\nSino Tohirzoda","html":"<p>東歐國家<br />\nElzbieta Martyniuk<br />\nPeter Maňka<br />\nSino Tohirzoda</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"拉丁美洲與加勒比海國家\nTeresa Dolores Cruz Sardiñas\nJosé Alfredo Hernández Ugalde","html":"<p>拉丁美洲與加勒比海國家<br />\nTeresa Dolores Cruz Sardiñas<br />\nJosé Alfredo Hernández Ugalde</p>","en":[10,11,12,13,14]},{"md":"西歐及其他國家\nMarcus Schroeder\nKatie Beckett\nMery Ciacci","html":"<p>西歐及其他國家<br />\nMarcus Schroeder<br />\nKatie Beckett<br />\nMery Ciacci</p>","en":[15,16,17]},{"md":"原住民族與地方社區\nViviana Elsa Figueroa","html":"<p>原住民族與地方社區<br />\nViviana Elsa Figueroa</p>","en":[18,19,20,21]},{"md":"項目 1\n會議開幕\n2. 會議由名古屋議定書下之遵約委員會卸任主席 Betty Kauna Schröder 開幕。Schröder 女士在開幕致詞中注意到","html":"<p>項目 1<br />\n會議開幕<br />\n2. 會議由名古屋議定書下之遵約委員會卸任主席 Betty Kauna Schröder 開幕。Schröder 女士在開幕致詞中注意到</p>","en":[22]},{"md":"* CBD/NP/MOP/6/1.","html":"<ul>\n<li>CBD/NP/MOP/6/1.</li>\n</ul>","en":[22]}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2/p002.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3"},{"t":"submission of the first national reports marked the first time in many years that the Committee had new and comprehensive information from Parties on the status of implementation, which would inform the work of the Committee moving forward. She also conveyed how much of an honour it had been for her to serve as Chair of the Committee."},{"t":"3.    The Committee was also addressed by the Executive Secretary of the Convention on Biological Diversity, Astrid Schomaker, who welcomed the participants to the meeting, thanked the outgoing Chair and drew the attention of the Committee to the analysis for the second assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Nagoya Protocol, which they would be considering. Ms. Schomaker noted that, while progress had been made, further work remained to be done, including changing perceptions surrounding the Protocol so that it could be viewed as a robust instrument for achieving the conservation and sustainable use of biological diversity."},{"t":"4.     A representative of the Secretariat reported that, with 13 members present, there was a quorum for the meeting to proceed, in accordance with section B, paragraph 10, of the cooperative procedures and institutional mechanisms to promote compliance with the provisions of the Nagoya Protocol and to address cases of non-compliance.1"},{"t":"Item 2"},{"t":"Organizational matters"},{"t":"(a)    Election of officers"},{"t":"5.    In section B, paragraph 9, of the cooperative procedures and institutional mechanisms, it is provided that the Compliance Committee shall elect its Chair and a Vice-Chair, who will rotate among the five regional groups of the United Nations."},{"t":"6.    Rule 12 (2) of the rules of procedure for the meetings of the Committee provides that the Chair and Vice-Chair shall be elected for a period of two years and that no officer shall serve for more than two consecutive terms."},{"t":"7.   As the outgoing Chair and Vice-Chair had served two consecutive terms in those roles, the Committee was invited to elect a new chair and a vice-chair. The Committee elected Elzbieta Martyniuk as Chair and José Alfredo Hernández Ugalde as Vice-Chair."},{"t":"8.     The Chair thanked the Committee for the trust that it had placed in her and the Secretariat for its work in preparing for the meeting."},{"t":"(b)    Adoption of the agenda"},{"t":"9.   The Compliance Committee adopted the agenda for the meeting, as contained in document CBD/NP/CC/5/1."},{"t":"(c)    Organization of work"},{"t":"10. The Compliance Committee approved the organization of work proposed by the Secretariat, as contained in annex I to the annotated provisional agenda.2 It was agreed that consideration of item 4 would be split into two parts, with the part addressing information from the second assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Protocol to follow consideration of agenda item 5."},{"t":"11. The Committee expressed its appreciation to the Secretariat for the high quality of the documents prepared for the meeting."},{"t":"Item 3"},{"t":"Outcomes of the fifth meeting of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the"},{"t":"1 Decision NP-1/4, annex."},{"t":"2 CBD/NP/CC/5/1/Add.1."},{"t":"2/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"第一份國家報告的提交，標誌著多年來委員會首次獲得締約方關於執行狀況的新且全面的資訊，這將為委員會未來的作業提供參考。她亦表示，能擔任委員會主席是她的榮幸。","html":"<p>第一份國家報告的提交，標誌著多年來委員會首次獲得締約方關於執行狀況的新且全面的資訊，這將為委員會未來的作業提供參考。她亦表示，能擔任委員會主席是她的榮幸。</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"3. 此外，生物多樣性公約執行秘書 Astrid Schomaker 向委員會發表了致詞，她歡迎會議參與者，感謝卸任主席，並提醒委員會注意關於名古屋議定書有效性第二次評估與審查的分析報告，委員會將對此進行審議。Schomaker 女士指出，雖然已取得進展，但仍有後續工作待完成，包括改變對議定書的認知，使其能被視為達成生物多樣性保育與永續利用之穩健工具。","html":"<p>3. 此外，生物多樣性公約執行秘書 Astrid Schomaker 向委員會發表了致詞，她歡迎會議參與者，感謝卸任主席，並提醒委員會注意關於名古屋議定書有效性第二次評估與審查的分析報告，委員會將對此進行審議。Schomaker 女士指出，雖然已取得進展，但仍有後續工作待完成，包括改變對議定書的認知，使其能被視為達成生物多樣性保育與永續利用之穩健工具。</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"4. 秘書處代表報告，在有 13 名成員出席的情況下，根據促進遵守名古屋議定書規定及處理不遵約案件之合作程序與制度機制 B 節第 10 段，會議已達法定人數，可以進行。1","html":"<p>4. 秘書處代表報告，在有 13 名成員出席的情況下，根據促進遵守名古屋議定書規定及處理不遵約案件之合作程序與制度機制 B 節第 10 段，會議已達法定人數，可以進行。1</p>","en":[3,4,5]},{"md":"議程第 2 項\n組織事項\n(a)\n官員選舉\n5. 在促進遵守名古屋議定書規定及處理不遵約案件之合作程序與制度機制 B 節第 9 段中規定，遵約委員會應選舉其主席及一名副主席，且該職位將在聯合國五個區域集團之間輪替。\n6. 委員會會議議事規則第 12 條第 (2) 款規定，主席與副主席之任期為兩年，且任何官員不得連續擔任超過兩屆。\n7. 由於卸任主席與副主席已連續擔任兩屆該職務，因此邀請委員會選舉新的主席與副主席。委員會選舉 Elzbieta Martyniuk 為主席，José Alfredo Hernández Ugalde 為副主席。\n8. 主席感謝委員會對其信任，並感謝秘書處為籌備會議所做的努力。","html":"<p>議程第 2 項<br />\n組織事項<br />\n(a)<br />\n官員選舉<br />\n5. 在促進遵守名古屋議定書規定及處理不遵約案件之合作程序與制度機制 B 節第 9 段中規定，遵約委員會應選舉其主席及一名副主席，且該職位將在聯合國五個區域集團之間輪替。<br />\n6. 委員會會議議事規則第 12 條第 (2) 款規定，主席與副主席之任期為兩年，且任何官員不得連續擔任超過兩屆。<br />\n7. 由於卸任主席與副主席已連續擔任兩屆該職務，因此邀請委員會選舉新的主席與副主席。委員會選舉 Elzbieta Martyniuk 為主席，José Alfredo Hernández Ugalde 為副主席。<br />\n8. 主席感謝委員會對其信任，並感謝秘書處為籌備會議所做的努力。</p>","en":[6,7,8,9,10]},{"md":"(b)\n議程通過\n9. 遵約委員會通過了會議議程，如文件 CBD/NP/CC/5/1 所載。","html":"<p>(b)<br />\n議程通過<br />\n9. 遵約委員會通過了會議議程，如文件 CBD/NP/CC/5/1 所載。</p>","en":[11,12,13]},{"md":"(c)\n工作組織\n10. 遵約委員會批准了秘書處所提議的工作組織，如附註臨時議程附件 I 所載。2 會議同意將議程第 4 項分為兩部分進行，其中處理議定書有效性第二次評估與審查資訊的部分，將在審議議程第 5 項之後進行。\n11. 委員會對秘書處為會議準備之文件的高品質表示感謝。","html":"<p>(c)<br />\n工作組織<br />\n10. 遵約委員會批准了秘書處所提議的工作組織，如附註臨時議程附件 I 所載。2 會議同意將議程第 4 項分為兩部分進行，其中處理議定書有效性第二次評估與審查資訊的部分，將在審議議程第 5 項之後進行。<br />\n11. 委員會對秘書處為會議準備之文件的高品質表示感謝。</p>","en":[14]},{"md":"議程第 3 項\n作為名古屋議定書締約方大會暨名古屋議定書會議第五屆會議之成果","html":"<p>議程第 3 項<br />\n作為名古屋議定書締約方大會暨名古屋議定書會議第五屆會議之成果</p>","en":[15,16]},{"md":"---\n1 決議 NP-1/4，附件。\n2 CBD/NP/CC/5/1/Add.1。","html":"<hr />\n<p>1 決議 NP-1/4，附件。<br />\n2 CBD/NP/CC/5/1/Add.1。</p>","en":[17,18,19,20]}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2/p003.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3"},{"t":"Parties to the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization regarding items relevant to compliance"},{"t":"12.    A representative of the Secretariat introduced document CBD/NP/CC/5/2."},{"t":"13. The Compliance Committee welcomed the positive consideration of its recommendations by the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol at its fifth meeting. It recognized that the amendments made by the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol had strengthened the text that had been recommended by the Committee."},{"t":"14. The Committee agreed that it would be beneficial for regions to coordinate ahead of meetings of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol and come prepared with information on their nominees for election to the Committee."},{"t":"Item 4"},{"t":"Review of general issues of compliance"},{"t":"15. A representative of the Secretariat introduced document CBD/NP/CC/5/3 and indicated that, since the preparation of the document, one additional Party (from Latin American and Caribbean States) had submitted its first national report. She also indicated that the United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP) was planning in-country support sessions to assist Parties that were participants in the Global Environment Facility (GEF)-funded project on support for the preparation and submission of the first national report on implementation of the Nagoya Protocol but that had not yet submitted their first national report."},{"t":"16. The Compliance Committee noted that, pursuant to its request at its fourth meeting, the Executive Secretary had sent letters to 103 Parties that had not yet adopted access and benefit-sharing measures, established the required institutional arrangements or published available information on the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House. About 20 per cent of those Parties acknowledged receipt, responded or took action following receipt of the original letter."},{"t":"17. The Committee expressed its appreciation to those Parties that had responded to the letters and taken action. The Committee expressed concern, however, at the low response rate to the letters and recalled that, under Article 13 of the Protocol, national focal points were responsible for liaison with the Secretariat. The Committee discussed possible reasons why Parties might not have responded to the letters (for example, insufficient capacity and resources, lack of political priority and absence of the necessary authority to respond to the letter) and possible follow-up actions."},{"t":"18. The Committee welcomed the high rate of submission of first national reports on the implementation of the Nagoya Protocol. The Committee expressed its appreciation for the capacity-building materials and activities to support Parties’ understanding of the reporting requirements and facilitate the submission of the reports provided by the Secretariat, including in collaboration with the UNEP-GEF project on support for the preparation and submission of the first national reports."},{"t":"19. The Committee requested the Secretariat to send letters to Parties that had not yet submitted their first national report to remind them of their obligation to do so and urge them to submit their report as soon as possible and no later than the date of the sixth meeting of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol. The Committee requested its Chair, as a second step, to send letters to the Parties concerned in the case where no response to the letters sent by the Secretariat had been received and no report had been submitted."},{"t":"20. The Committee agreed on several recommendations regarding national reporting and the financial mechanism for consideration by the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol, as set out in annex I to the present report."},{"t":"21. On the basis of information from the second assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Protocol, the Committee reviewed general issues of compliance with the obligations to establish legislative, administrative or policy measures on access and benefit-sharing; put in place institutional"},{"t":"3/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其所產生利益之名古屋議定書》中與遵約相關事項之締約方","html":"<p>關於《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其所產生利益之名古屋議定書》中與遵約相關事項之締約方</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"12. 秘書處代表介紹了文件 CBD/NP/CC/5/2。","html":"<p>12. 秘書處代表介紹了文件 CBD/NP/CC/5/2。</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"13. 遵約委員會**歡迎**擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會在其第五屆會議中，對其建議所進行的積極考量。委員會認可擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會所做的修訂，強化了委員會所建議之文本。","html":"<p>13. 遵約委員會<strong>歡迎</strong>擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會在其第五屆會議中，對其建議所進行的積極考量。委員會認可擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會所做的修訂，強化了委員會所建議之文本。</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"14. 委員會同意，各區域在擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會會議之前進行協調，並準備好其擬選舉至委員會之提名人資訊，將是有益的。","html":"<p>14. 委員會同意，各區域在擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會會議之前進行協調，並準備好其擬選舉至委員會之提名人資訊，將是有益的。</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"項目 4\n遵約一般議題之審查","html":"<p>項目 4<br />\n遵約一般議題之審查</p>","en":[5,6]},{"md":"15. 秘書處代表介紹了文件 CBD/NP/CC/5/3，並指出自該文件編製以來，又有一位額外的締約方（來自拉丁美洲及加勒比海國家）提交了其第一份國家報告。她亦指出，聯合國環境規劃署（UNEP）正計畫進行國內支援會議，以協助那些參與了由全球環境基金（GEF）資助之「支援編製與提交名古屋議定書實施第一份國家報告」計畫，但尚未提交其第一份國家報告之締約方。","html":"<p>15. 秘書處代表介紹了文件 CBD/NP/CC/5/3，並指出自該文件編製以來，又有一位額外的締約方（來自拉丁美洲及加勒比海國家）提交了其第一份國家報告。她亦指出，聯合國環境規劃署（UNEP）正計畫進行國內支援會議，以協助那些參與了由全球環境基金（GEF）資助之「支援編製與提交名古屋議定書實施第一份國家報告」計畫，但尚未提交其第一份國家報告之締約方。</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"16. 遵約委員會**注意到**，根據其在第四屆會議上的請求，執行秘書已致函 103 個尚未採取取得與利益分享措施、尚未建立必要制度安排或尚未於取得與利益分享資訊交換所（Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House）發布可用資訊之締約方。在這些締約方中，約有 20% 在收到原信函後確認收到、作出回應或採取了行動。","html":"<p>16. 遵約委員會<strong>注意到</strong>，根據其在第四屆會議上的請求，執行秘書已致函 103 個尚未採取取得與利益分享措施、尚未建立必要制度安排或尚未於取得與利益分享資訊交換所（Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House）發布可用資訊之締約方。在這些締約方中，約有 20% 在收到原信函後確認收到、作出回應或採取了行動。</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"17. 委員會對那些已回應信函並採取行動之締約方表示感謝。然而，委員會對信函的回應率偏低表示關切，並**回顧**，根據議定書第 13 條，國家聯絡點負責與秘書處進行聯絡。委員會討論了締約方可能未回應信函之可能原因（例如：能力與資源不足、缺乏政治優先權以及缺乏回應信函之必要權限）以及可能的後續行動。","html":"<p>17. 委員會對那些已回應信函並採取行動之締約方表示感謝。然而，委員會對信函的回應率偏低表示關切，並<strong>回顧</strong>，根據議定書第 13 條，國家聯絡點負責與秘書處進行聯絡。委員會討論了締約方可能未回應信函之可能原因（例如：能力與資源不足、缺乏政治優先權以及缺乏回應信函之必要權限）以及可能的後續行動。</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"18. 委員會**歡迎**提交名古屋議定書實施第一份國家報告的高比例。委員會對秘書處所提供之、旨在支持締約方理解報告要求並促進報告提交之能力建構教材與活動表示感謝，包括與「支援編製與提交第一份國家報告」之 UNEP-GEF 計畫合作所進行之活動。","html":"<p>18. 委員會<strong>歡迎</strong>提交名古屋議定書實施第一份國家報告的高比例。委員會對秘書處所提供之、旨在支持締約方理解報告要求並促進報告提交之能力建構教材與活動表示感謝，包括與「支援編製與提交第一份國家報告」之 UNEP-GEF 計畫合作所進行之活動。</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"19. 委員會**請求**秘書處致函尚未提交其第一份國家報告之締約方，以提醒其履行該義務，並**敦促**其盡快且不遲於擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會第六屆會議之日期提交其報告。委員會**請求**其主席作為第二步，在秘書處發出的信函未收到回應且未提交報告的情況下，致函相關締約方。","html":"<p>19. 委員會<strong>請求</strong>秘書處致函尚未提交其第一份國家報告之締約方，以提醒其履行該義務，並<strong>敦促</strong>其盡快且不遲於擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會第六屆會議之日期提交其報告。委員會<strong>請求</strong>其主席作為第二步，在秘書處發出的信函未收到回應且未提交報告的情況下，致函相關締約方。</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"20. 委員會就國家報告與財務機制達成若干建議，以供擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會審議，如本報告附件 I 所列。","html":"<p>20. 委員會就國家報告與財務機制達成若干建議，以供擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會審議，如本報告附件 I 所列。</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"21. 根據對議定書有效性進行第二次評估與審查之資訊，委員會審查了關於履行建立取得與利益分享之立法、行政或政策措施；建立","html":"<p>21. 根據對議定書有效性進行第二次評估與審查之資訊，委員會審查了關於履行建立取得與利益分享之立法、行政或政策措施；建立</p>","en":[13,14]}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2/p004.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3"},{"t":"structures required under the Protocol; and publish information on the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House."},{"t":"22. The Committee recognized that 74 per cent of Parties had established one or more competent national authorities. Given the central role of competent national authorities, however, further efforts were needed to advance compliance with that obligation. Moreover, the Committee expressed concern that only 46 per cent of Parties had designated one or more checkpoints and that nearly 50 per cent of Parties had indicated that they had information that had not yet been published on the Clearing-House."},{"t":"23. The Committee agreed on several recommendations regarding compliance for consideration by the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol, as set out in annex I to the present report."},{"t":"24.   The Committee requested its Chair to send letters to Parties:"},{"t":"(a) That had indicated that they had information that had not yet been published on the Clearing-House, reminding them of their obligation to publish such information;"},{"t":"(b) That had not yet taken measures to implement the Protocol or had not yet designated a national focal point, competent national authority or checkpoint, reminding them of their obligation to do so."},{"t":"25. The Committee agreed that, at its next meeting, it would review consistency between information contained in the national reports and information published on the Clearing-House, with a view to identifying specific gaps and enabling targeted and supportive follow-up consistent with the Committee’s facilitative mandate."},{"t":"Item 5"},{"t":"Input to the second assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Nagoya Protocol"},{"t":"26. A representative of the Secretariat introduced documents CBD/NP/CC/5/4, CBD/NP/CC/5/4/Add.1 and CBD/NP/CC/5/4/Add.2 and gave a presentation on the methodology used for conducting the second assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Protocol. The representative described how the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol had decided to conduct the second assessment and review on the basis of the elements listed in the annex to decision NP-5/5. The representative also described the framework of indicators agreed to in annex II to decision NP-3/1 and the reference points contained therein to be used as a baseline against which progress on each element could be measured."},{"t":"27. The Compliance Committee noted that it was to work in a complementary and non-duplicative manner with the Informal Advisory Committee on Capacity-building for the Implementation of the Nagoya Protocol and, accordingly, it would consider element (a), sections 2, 3, 4, 5 and 7, and element (g), section 1, on the basis of document CBD/NP/CC/5/4/Add.1; and element (j) on the basis of document CBD/NP/CC/5/4/Add.2. The Compliance Committee discussed the allocation of elements between the two bodies and noted the relevance of Article 8 of the Protocol to its work."},{"t":"28.     The Compliance Committee noted that, while the indicator data highlighted progress made by Parties in establishing institutional structures and putting access and benefit-sharing measures in place since the first assessment and review of the Protocol in 2018, the data did not reflect whether those institutions and measures were operational or effective in accomplishing the objectives of the Protocol. The Committee also noted that the wording for some of the indicators related to access (for example, issuance of permits or internationally recognized certificates of compliance) could be adjusted so that they would be measured based on the number of Parties that had required prior informed consent instead of on the total number of Parties to the Protocol."},{"t":"29. The Committee discussed the different approaches taken by Parties with respect to responding to the questions of the first national report related to implementation of Article 5 of the Protocol, as"},{"t":"4/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"議定書所要求之制度結構；並於取得與利益分享資訊交換所發布資訊。\n22. 委員會認可 74% 的締約方已設立一個或多個國家主管機關。然而，鑑於國家主管機關的核心角色，仍需進一步努力以推進履行該義務。此外，委員會對僅有 46% 的締約方指定了一個或多個檢查點，且近 50% 的締約方表示其擁有尚未於資訊交換所發布之資訊表示關切。\n23. 委員會就關於遵約的若干建議達成一致，以供擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會審議，如本報告附件 I 所列。\n24. 委員會**請求**其主席向下列締約方發函：\n(a) 表示其擁有尚未於資訊交換所發布之資訊者，提醒其發布此類資訊之義務；\n(b) 尚未採取措施實施議定書，或尚未指定國家聯絡點、國家主管機關或檢查點者，提醒其履行該義務。\n25. 委員會達成一致，將於下次會議審查國家報告中所含資訊與資訊交換所發布資訊之間的一致性，旨在識別特定差距，並在符合委員會促進性職能之情況下，進行具針對性且具支持性的後續追蹤。","html":"<p>議定書所要求之制度結構；並於取得與利益分享資訊交換所發布資訊。<br />\n22. 委員會認可 74% 的締約方已設立一個或多個國家主管機關。然而，鑑於國家主管機關的核心角色，仍需進一步努力以推進履行該義務。此外，委員會對僅有 46% 的締約方指定了一個或多個檢查點，且近 50% 的締約方表示其擁有尚未於資訊交換所發布之資訊表示關切。<br />\n23. 委員會就關於遵約的若干建議達成一致，以供擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會審議，如本報告附件 I 所列。<br />\n24. 委員會<strong>請求</strong>其主席向下列締約方發函：<br />\n(a) 表示其擁有尚未於資訊交換所發布之資訊者，提醒其發布此類資訊之義務；<br />\n(b) 尚未採取措施實施議定書，或尚未指定國家聯絡點、國家主管機關或檢查點者，提醒其履行該義務。<br />\n25. 委員會達成一致，將於下次會議審查國家報告中所含資訊與資訊交換所發布資訊之間的一致性，旨在識別特定差距，並在符合委員會促進性職能之情況下，進行具針對性且具支持性的後續追蹤。</p>","en":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"md":"項目 5\n針對名古屋議定書有效性第二次評估與審查之投入\n26. 秘書處代表介紹了文件 CBD/NP/CC/5/4、CBD/NP/CC/5/4/Add.1 及 CBD/NP/CC/5/4/Add.2，並就進行議定書有效性第二次評估與審查所使用之方法論進行了簡報。該代表說明了擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會，如何根據決議 NP-5/5 附件中所列要素，決定進行第二次評估與審查。該代表亦說明了決議 NP-3/1 附件 II 中達成一致之指標架構，以及其中包含作為基準之參考點，用以衡量各要素之進展。\n27. 遵約委員會**注意到**，其應與「名古屋議定書實施能力建構非正式諮詢委員會」以互補且不重複之方式合作，因此，將根據文件 CBD/NP/CC/5/4/Add.1，審議要素 (a) 第 2、3、4、5 及 7 小節，以及要素 (g) 第 1 小節；並根據文件 CBD/NP/CC/5/4/Add.2，審議要素 (j)。遵約委員會討論了兩機構之間要素分配之情形，並注意到議定書第 8 條與其工作之相關性。\n28. 遵約委員會**注意到**，雖然指標資料凸顯了締約方自 2018 年議定書第一次評估與審查以來，在建立制度結構及落實取得與利益分享措施方面所取得之進展，但該資料並未反映這些制度與措施在達成議定書目標方面是否具備運作性或有效性。委員會亦**注意到**，部分與取得相關之指標（例如：核發許可證或國際公認之遵約證明）之措辭可以進行調整，使其改為根據要求事先知情同意之締約方數量，而非根據議定書締約方之總數來進行衡量。\n29. 委員會討論了締約方在回應與議定書第 5 條實施相關之第一份國家報告問題時所採取的不同方法，","html":"<p>項目 5<br />\n針對名古屋議定書有效性第二次評估與審查之投入<br />\n26. 秘書處代表介紹了文件 CBD/NP/CC/5/4、CBD/NP/CC/5/4/Add.1 及 CBD/NP/CC/5/4/Add.2，並就進行議定書有效性第二次評估與審查所使用之方法論進行了簡報。該代表說明了擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會，如何根據決議 NP-5/5 附件中所列要素，決定進行第二次評估與審查。該代表亦說明了決議 NP-3/1 附件 II 中達成一致之指標架構，以及其中包含作為基準之參考點，用以衡量各要素之進展。<br />\n27. 遵約委員會<strong>注意到</strong>，其應與「名古屋議定書實施能力建構非正式諮詢委員會」以互補且不重複之方式合作，因此，將根據文件 CBD/NP/CC/5/4/Add.1，審議要素 (a) 第 2、3、4、5 及 7 小節，以及要素 (g) 第 1 小節；並根據文件 CBD/NP/CC/5/4/Add.2，審議要素 (j)。遵約委員會討論了兩機構之間要素分配之情形，並注意到議定書第 8 條與其工作之相關性。<br />\n28. 遵約委員會<strong>注意到</strong>，雖然指標資料凸顯了締約方自 2018 年議定書第一次評估與審查以來，在建立制度結構及落實取得與利益分享措施方面所取得之進展，但該資料並未反映這些制度與措施在達成議定書目標方面是否具備運作性或有效性。委員會亦<strong>注意到</strong>，部分與取得相關之指標（例如：核發許可證或國際公認之遵約證明）之措辭可以進行調整，使其改為根據要求事先知情同意之締約方數量，而非根據議定書締約方之總數來進行衡量。<br />\n29. 委員會討論了締約方在回應與議定書第 5 條實施相關之第一份國家報告問題時所採取的不同方法，</p>","en":[9,10,11,12,13]}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2/p005.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3"},{"t":"explained in paragraph 49 of document CBD/NP/CC/5/4/Add.1. The Committee noted that it might be useful to provide more clarity on what type of measures on fair and equitable benefit-sharing Parties had adopted in subsequent national reports."},{"t":"30. In the context of element (g), the Committee noted that while the publication of checkpoint communiqués should apply to genetic resources coming from another country, some Parties had published certificates for access to and checkpoint communiqués for utilization of genetic resources by domestic users. It therefore suggested that a distinction could be created on the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House between certificates and checkpoint communiqués for domestic users and those for users in another country."},{"t":"31. For elements (a) and (g), the Committee agreed on key findings and messages; indicative actions that could be taken at the national level to enhance the implementation of the Protocol; and actions that could be taken at the global or regional level to enhance the implementation of the Protocol, as set out below in annexes II, III and IV, respectively, as its inputs to the second assessment and review."},{"t":"32. For element (j), the Committee recognized that experience with the cooperative procedures and institutional mechanisms on compliance was limited to date and that it had not fully explored the tools at its disposal as provided for under the cooperative procedures and institutional mechanisms. That finding is reflected in annex II below."},{"t":"Item 6"},{"t":"Other matters"},{"t":"33. Under agenda item 6, the Secretariat recalled that five seats (one per region) in the Compliance Committee would be up for election at the sixth meeting of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol."},{"t":"Item 7"},{"t":"Adoption of the report"},{"t":"34.    The Chair introduced the draft report of the meeting, which was adopted, as orally amended."},{"t":"Item 8"},{"t":"Closure of the meeting"},{"t":"35. Following the customary exchange of courtesies, the meeting was closed at 5.40 p.m. on 29 May 2026."},{"t":"5/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"如文件 CBD/NP/CC/5/4/Add.1 第 49 段所述。委員會注意到，針對締約方在隨後國家報告中所採取的公平公正利益分享措施類型，提供更明確的說明可能會有用。\n30. 在要素 (g) 的背景下，委員會注意到，雖然檢查點公報的發布應適用於來自另一國家的遺傳資源，但若干締約方已針對國內使用者對遺傳資源的取得與利用，發布了取得證明書與檢查點公報。因此，委員會建議可在取得與利益分享資訊交換所中，針對國內使用者的證明書與檢查點公報，以及針對另一國使用者的證明書與檢查點公報，建立區分。\n31. 針對要素 (a) 與 (g)，委員會就其作為第二次評估與審查之投入內容，就關鍵發現與訊息、為加強議定書執行而在國家層級可採取的示意性行動，以及為加強議定書執行而在全球或區域層級可採取的行動，達成一致，分別如附件 II、III 及 IV 所列。\n32. 針對要素 (j)，委員會認可迄今為止關於遵約之合作程序與制度機制的經驗有限，且尚未充分探索其在合作程序與制度機制下所擁有的工具。該發現反映在下方的附件 II 中。","html":"<p>如文件 CBD/NP/CC/5/4/Add.1 第 49 段所述。委員會注意到，針對締約方在隨後國家報告中所採取的公平公正利益分享措施類型，提供更明確的說明可能會有用。<br />\n30. 在要素 (g) 的背景下，委員會注意到，雖然檢查點公報的發布應適用於來自另一國家的遺傳資源，但若干締約方已針對國內使用者對遺傳資源的取得與利用，發布了取得證明書與檢查點公報。因此，委員會建議可在取得與利益分享資訊交換所中，針對國內使用者的證明書與檢查點公報，以及針對另一國使用者的證明書與檢查點公報，建立區分。<br />\n31. 針對要素 (a) 與 (g)，委員會就其作為第二次評估與審查之投入內容，就關鍵發現與訊息、為加強議定書執行而在國家層級可採取的示意性行動，以及為加強議定書執行而在全球或區域層級可採取的行動，達成一致，分別如附件 II、III 及 IV 所列。<br />\n32. 針對要素 (j)，委員會認可迄今為止關於遵約之合作程序與制度機制的經驗有限，且尚未充分探索其在合作程序與制度機制下所擁有的工具。該發現反映在下方的附件 II 中。</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"項目 6\n其他事項\n33. 在議程項目 6 下，秘書處回顧，遵約委員會中五個席位（每個區域一個）將於擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會第六屆會議時進行選舉。","html":"<p>項目 6<br />\n其他事項<br />\n33. 在議程項目 6 下，秘書處回顧，遵約委員會中五個席位（每個區域一個）將於擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會第六屆會議時進行選舉。</p>","en":[5,6,7]},{"md":"項目 7\n報告之通過\n34. 主席介紹了會議報告草案，該草案經口頭修正後獲得通過。","html":"<p>項目 7<br />\n報告之通過<br />\n34. 主席介紹了會議報告草案，該草案經口頭修正後獲得通過。</p>","en":[8,9,10]},{"md":"項目 8\n會議閉幕\n35. 在慣常的禮節性交流後，會議於 2026 年 5 月 29 日下午 5.40 閉幕。","html":"<p>項目 8<br />\n會議閉幕<br />\n35. 在慣常的禮節性交流後，會議於 2026 年 5 月 29 日下午 5.40 閉幕。</p>","en":[11,12,13,14]}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2/p006.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3"},{"t":"Annex I"},{"t":"Recommendations of the Compliance Committee for consideration at the sixth"},{"t":"meeting of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and"},{"t":"Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization"},{"t":"I.        Compliance"},{"t":"1.    The Compliance Committee recommends that, at its sixth meeting, the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization to the Convention on Biological Diversity adopt a decision along the following lines:"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol"},{"t":"1.   Welcomes the progress made by Parties in the implementation of the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization to the Convention on Biological Diversity;1"},{"t":"2.    Recognizes that further work is needed to advance the implementation of the Protocol;"},{"t":"3.    Expresses concern that:"},{"t":"(a) Twenty-six per cent of Parties have not yet designated one or more competent national authorities and 54 per cent of Parties have not yet designated one or more checkpoints, indicating significant gaps in the institutional and monitoring architecture of the Protocol;2"},{"t":"(b) Nearly 50 per cent of Parties indicated that they had information that had not yet been published on the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House, pointing to a gap in fulfilling the requirements under Article 14 of the Protocol;3"},{"t":"4.     Urges Parties that have not yet done so to establish legislative, administrative and policy measures and institutional arrangements for implementing the Protocol, publish as soon as possible all available information required under Article 14 of the Protocol through the Clearing-House and keep such information updated as required;"},{"t":"5.    Requests that Parties collaborate fully when requested to provide information related to their compliance with obligations under the Protocol;"},{"t":"6.    Welcomes the contribution of the Compliance Committee under the Nagoya Protocol to the second assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Protocol."},{"t":"II. Monitoring and reporting"},{"t":"2.    The Compliance Committee also recommends that, at its sixth meeting, the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol adopt a decision that includes the following elements:"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol"},{"t":"1.    Welcomes the first national reports submitted;"},{"t":"1 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 3008, No. 30619."},{"t":"2 See CBD/SBI/7/7/Add.1."},{"t":"3 Ibid."},{"t":"6/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"附件 I\n遵約委員會建議，供擔任《關於取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生利益公平公正分享之名古屋議定書》締約方會議之締約方大會第六屆會議審議","html":"<p>附件 I<br />\n遵約委員會建議，供擔任《關於取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生利益公平公正分享之名古屋議定書》締約方會議之締約方大會第六屆會議審議</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"I. 遵約","html":"<p>I. 遵約</p>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]},{"md":"1. 遵約委員會建議，於其第六屆會議中，擔任《關於取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生利益公平公正分享之名古屋議定書》締約方會議之締約方大會，應通過如下內容之決議：\n擔任《關於取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生利益公平公正分享之名古屋議定書》締約方會議之締約方大會\n1. **歡迎**締約方在履行《關於取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生利益公平公正分享之名古屋議定書》方面所取得的進展；¹\n2. **認識到**需要進一步的工作以推進議定書的履行；\n3. **表示關切**：\n(a) 26% 的締約方尚未指定一個或多個國家主管機關，且 54% 的締約方尚未指定一個或多個檢查點，顯示議定書在制度與監測架構方面存在重大差距；²\n(b) 近 50% 的締約方表示其擁有尚未在取得與利益分享資訊交換所發布的資訊，指出在履行議定書第 14 條規定之要求方面存在差距；³\n4. **敦促**尚未採取行動的締約方建立履行議定書所需的立法、行政與政策措施及制度安排，並盡快透過資訊交換所發布議定書第 14 條所要求的所有可用資訊，並按要求保持該等資訊之更新；\n5. **請求**締約方在被要求提供與其履行議定書義務相關之資訊時，應充分合作；\n6. **歡迎**《名古屋議定書》下遵約委員會對議定書有效性第二次評估與審查所做的貢獻。","html":"<p>1. 遵約委員會建議，於其第六屆會議中，擔任《關於取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生利益公平公正分享之名古屋議定書》締約方會議之締約方大會，應通過如下內容之決議：<br />\n擔任《關於取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生利益公平公正分享之名古屋議定書》締約方會議之締約方大會<br />\n1. <strong>歡迎</strong>締約方在履行《關於取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生利益公平公正分享之名古屋議定書》方面所取得的進展；¹<br />\n2. <strong>認識到</strong>需要進一步的工作以推進議定書的履行；<br />\n3. <strong>表示關切</strong>：<br />\n(a) 26% 的締約方尚未指定一個或多個國家主管機關，且 54% 的締約方尚未指定一個或多個檢查點，顯示議定書在制度與監測架構方面存在重大差距；²<br />\n(b) 近 50% 的締約方表示其擁有尚未在取得與利益分享資訊交換所發布的資訊，指出在履行議定書第 14 條規定之要求方面存在差距；³<br />\n4. <strong>敦促</strong>尚未採取行動的締約方建立履行議定書所需的立法、行政與政策措施及制度安排，並盡快透過資訊交換所發布議定書第 14 條所要求的所有可用資訊，並按要求保持該等資訊之更新；<br />\n5. <strong>請求</strong>締約方在被要求提供與其履行議定書義務相關之資訊時，應充分合作；<br />\n6. <strong>歡迎</strong>《名古屋議定書》下遵約委員會對議定書有效性第二次評估與審查所做的貢獻。</p>","en":[10,11,12,13,14]},{"md":"II. 監測與報告\n2. 遵約委員會亦建議，於其第六屆會議中，擔任《名古屋議定書》締約方會議之締約方大會，應通過包含下列要素之決議：\n擔任《名古屋議定書》締約方會議之締約方大會\n1. **歡迎**提交的首份國家報告；","html":"<p>II. 監測與報告<br />\n2. 遵約委員會亦建議，於其第六屆會議中，擔任《名古屋議定書》締約方會議之締約方大會，應通過包含下列要素之決議：<br />\n擔任《名古屋議定書》締約方會議之締約方大會<br />\n1. <strong>歡迎</strong>提交的首份國家報告；</p>","en":[15,16,17]},{"md":"¹ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 3008, No. 30619.\n² See CBD/SBI/7/7/Add.1.\n³ Ibid.","html":"<p>¹ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 3008, No. 30619.<br />\n² See CBD/SBI/7/7/Add.1.<br />\n³ Ibid.</p>","en":[18,19,20,21,22]}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2/p007.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3"},{"t":"2.        Urges Parties that have not yet submitted their first national reports to do so as soon as possible;"},{"t":"3.     Expresses its appreciation to the Global Environment Facility and the United Nations Environment Programme for the support provided to eligible Parties in the preparation and submission of their first national reports, and acknowledges the administrative challenges associated with the project development process and the resulting significant delay in the distribution of funds;"},{"t":"4.     Commends the efforts made by the Secretariat of the Convention on Biological Diversity4 to assist Parties in submitting their first national report;"},{"t":"5.     Urges Parties to monitor the implementation of their obligations under the Protocol pursuant to Article 29 with respect to facilitating the preparation and timely submission of the second national reports and explore opportunities for mobilizing resources in support of those activities."},{"t":"III. Financial mechanism"},{"t":"3.    The Compliance Committee further recommends that, at its sixth meeting, the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol adopt a decision that includes the following elements:"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol Recommends that, at its seventeenth meeting, the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity,5 in its guidance to the financial mechanism, request the Global Environment Facility to make funds available in a timely manner to support eligible Parties in the preparation and submission of their second national reports on the implementation of the Protocol and encourage the initiation of the associated project development process in 2027, with a view to securing project approval by the end of 2027 and enabling project activities, including any regional workshops, to be undertaken in 2028 and early 2029, well in advance of the expected reporting deadline."},{"t":"4 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"5 Ibid."},{"t":"7/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"2. **敦促**尚未提交其第一份國家報告之締約方盡快提交；","html":"<p>2. <strong>敦促</strong>尚未提交其第一份國家報告之締約方盡快提交；</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"3. **表示**感謝全球環境基金與聯合國環境規劃署對符合資格之締約方在編製與提交其第一份國家報告方面所提供之支持，並**注意到**與計畫開發程序相關之行政挑戰，以及由此導致之資金發放重大延遲；","html":"<p>3. <strong>表示</strong>感謝全球環境基金與聯合國環境規劃署對符合資格之締約方在編製與提交其第一份國家報告方面所提供之支持，並<strong>注意到</strong>與計畫開發程序相關之行政挑戰，以及由此導致之資金發放重大延遲；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"4. **讚揚**生物多樣性公約秘書處⁴為協助締約方提交其第一份國家報告所做出之努力；","html":"<p>4. <strong>讚揚</strong>生物多樣性公約秘書處⁴為協助締約方提交其第一份國家報告所做出之努力；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"5. **敦促**締約方根據第 29 條，針對促進第二份國家報告之編製與及時提交，監測其在議定書下義務之履行情況，並探索動員資源以支持該等活動之機會。","html":"<p>5. <strong>敦促</strong>締約方根據第 29 條，針對促進第二份國家報告之編製與及時提交，監測其在議定書下義務之履行情況，並探索動員資源以支持該等活動之機會。</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"III. 財務機制","html":"<p>III. 財務機制</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"3. 遵約委員會進一步**建議**，於其第六屆會議上，擔任名古屋議定書締約方會議之締約方大會應通過一項包含下列要素之決議：","html":"<p>3. 遵約委員會進一步<strong>建議</strong>，於其第六屆會議上，擔任名古屋議定書締約方會議之締約方大會應通過一項包含下列要素之決議：</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"擔任名古屋議定書締約方會議之締約方大會","html":"<p>擔任名古屋議定書締約方會議之締約方大會</p>","pre":"方大會應通過一項包含下列要素之決議：\n\n","en":[7]},{"md":"**建議**，於其第十七屆會議上，生物多樣性公約締約方大會⁵，在其對財務機制之指導中，**請求**全球環境基金及時提供資金，以支持符合資格之締約方編製與提交其關於履行議定書之第二份國家報告，並**鼓勵**於 2027 年啟動相關計畫開發程序，旨在於 2027 年底前獲得計畫核准，並使計畫活動（包括任何區域性工作坊）得以於 2028 年及 2029 年初進行，且遠早於預期之報告截止日期。","html":"<p><strong>建議</strong>，於其第十七屆會議上，生物多樣性公約締約方大會⁵，在其對財務機制之指導中，<strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金及時提供資金，以支持符合資格之締約方編製與提交其關於履行議定書之第二份國家報告，並<strong>鼓勵</strong>於 2027 年啟動相關計畫開發程序，旨在於 2027 年底前獲得計畫核准，並使計畫活動（包括任何區域性工作坊）得以於 2028 年及 2029 年初進行，且遠早於預期之報告截止日期。</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"⁴ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.\n⁵ 同上。","html":"<p>⁴ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.<br />\n⁵ 同上。</p>","en":[8,9,10]}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2/p008.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3"},{"t":"Annex II"},{"t":"Key findings and messages"},{"t":"Element (a): extent of implementation of the provisions of the Nagoya Protocol and related obligations of Parties, including assessment of progress by Parties in establishing institutional structures and access and benefit-sharing measures to implement the Protocol"},{"t":"1.     According to the updated indicator data, and in comparison with the data for February 2018, there has been significant progress in setting the legislative, administrative and policy foundations for advancing implementation of the Nagoya Protocol, including the designation of national focal points and competent national authorities and the adoption of legislative, administrative and policy measures on access and benefit-sharing, although progress has been uneven among regions. There are differences with regard to understanding of the role of checkpoints; their designation and operationalization constitute a challenge for many Parties; and the limited progress in that area is concerning. In that regard, information shows that many Parties still need to adopt further measures to render the Nagoya Protocol fully operational and translate principles into practice."},{"t":"2.      While indicator data highlight progress made by Parties in establishing institutional structures and putting access and benefit-sharing measures in place, the data do not elucidate whether those institutions and measures are operational or effective in accomplishing the objective of the Protocol. It is concerning that many Parties still have information available that has not yet been published on the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House, as required under Article 14 of the Protocol."},{"t":"3.    Insufficient human resources and capacity, the multiplicity of roles and responsibilities of national focal points and issues relating to internal coordination among different authorities or ministries or among competent national authorities and checkpoints are ongoing challenges."},{"t":"4.     While the indicators related to implementation of Article 6 show significant progress by Parties, the diversity of national approaches to requirements and procedures for access and benefit-sharing presents key challenges for users, including with respect to understanding the scope of application and terminology and the steps to be followed in acquiring prior informed consent and a permit and negotiating mutually agreed terms and sharing benefits. Furthermore, while the internationally recognized certificate of compliance is an important tool for providing legal certainty of access and supporting the monitoring of the utilization of genetic resources, to date, only a limited number of Parties with access measures in place have published permits on the Clearing-House that constitute such certificates."},{"t":"5.    Developing clear procedures (for example, step-by-step guidance for users on applicable rules and requirements), practical information and model contractual clauses and publishing them on the Clearing-House will allow the Clearing-House to be more effective in achieving its objective of providing users with key information about access to genetic resources and associated traditional knowledge and benefit-sharing."},{"t":"6.     Indicators related to Article 5 show significant progress made by Parties, even if they do not demonstrate whether the measures put in place are effective in accomplishing the objective of the Protocol. It should be noted that Parties followed different approaches in answering the relevant question of the report, with some Parties providing information on measures to ensure benefit-sharing from the utilization of genetic resources or associated traditional knowledge accessed within their jurisdiction (through requirements for prior informed consent and mutually agreed terms) and others providing information on measures to ensure benefit-sharing from the utilization of genetic resources and associated traditional knowledge accessed from other Parties (through the adoption of compliance measures) and still others addressing both approaches."},{"t":"7.    With regard to reducing negotiation-related asymmetries between providers, including indigenous peoples and local communities, and users of genetic resources, there is a need to enhance"},{"t":"8/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"附件 II\n關鍵發現與訊息\n要素 (a)：名古屋議定書條款之實施程度及締約方相關義務，包括締約方在建立制度結構及取得與利益分享措施以實施議定書方面之進展評估\n1. 根據更新後的指標資料，與 2018 年 2 月的資料相比，在建立推動名古屋議定書實施之立法、行政與政策基礎方面已取得顯著進展，包括指定國家聯絡點與國家主管機關，以及採取取得與利益分享之立法、行政與政策措施，儘管各區域之進展並不均衡。關於檢查點（checkpoints）角色之理解存在差異；其指定與運作對許多締約方而言構成挑戰；且該領域進展有限，令人擔憂。就此而言，資訊顯示許多締約方仍需採取進一步措施，以使名古屋議定書能完全運作，並將原則轉化為實踐。\n2. 雖然指標資料凸顯了締約方在建立制度結構及落實取得與利益分享措施方面所取得的進展，但資料並未闡明這些制度與措施在達成議定書目標方面是否已投入運作或具備成效。令人擔憂的是，許多締約方仍有資訊尚未依據議定書第 14 條之要求，發布於取得與利益分享資訊交換所。\n3. 人力資源與能力不足、國家聯絡點角色與責任之多樣性，以及不同主管機關或部會之間，或國家主管機關與檢查點之間內部協調之議題，仍是持續存在的挑戰。\n4. 雖然與第 6 條實施相關的指標顯示締約方已取得顯著進展，但各國對於取得與利益分享之要求與程序的做法多樣化，對使用者而言構成了關鍵挑戰，包括在理解適用範圍與術語，以及在取得事先知情同意與許可證、協商共同商定條件及分享利益之步驟方面。此外，雖然國際公認的合規證明是提供取得之法律確定性及支持遺傳資源利用監測的重要工具，但迄今為止，僅有少數已落實取得措施的締約方在資訊交換所上發布了構成此類證明的許可證。\n5. 制定清晰的程序（例如，為使用者提供適用規則與要求的逐步指南）、實用資訊及範本契約條款，並將其發布於資訊交換所，將使資訊交換所在達成其目標方面更具成效，即為使用者提供有關遺傳資源及其相關傳統知識之取得與利益分享的關鍵資訊。\n6. 與第 5 條相關的指標顯示締約方已取得顯著進展，即便這些指標並未證明已落實的措施在達成議定書目標方面是否有效。應注意的是，締約方在回答報告相關問題時採取了不同的方法，部分締約方提供了關於確保在其管轄範圍內取得之遺傳資源或相關傳統知識利用之利益分享措施的資訊（透過事先知情同意與共同商定條件之要求），其他締約方則提供了關於確保從其他締約方取得之遺傳資源與相關傳統知識利用之利益分享措施的資訊（透過採取合規措施），還有其他締約方則同時處理這兩種方法。\n7. 關於減少提供者（包括原住民族與地方社區）與遺傳資源使用者之間談判相關的不對稱性，有必要加強","html":"<p>附件 II<br />\n關鍵發現與訊息<br />\n要素 (a)：名古屋議定書條款之實施程度及締約方相關義務，包括締約方在建立制度結構及取得與利益分享措施以實施議定書方面之進展評估<br />\n1. 根據更新後的指標資料，與 2018 年 2 月的資料相比，在建立推動名古屋議定書實施之立法、行政與政策基礎方面已取得顯著進展，包括指定國家聯絡點與國家主管機關，以及採取取得與利益分享之立法、行政與政策措施，儘管各區域之進展並不均衡。關於檢查點（checkpoints）角色之理解存在差異；其指定與運作對許多締約方而言構成挑戰；且該領域進展有限，令人擔憂。就此而言，資訊顯示許多締約方仍需採取進一步措施，以使名古屋議定書能完全運作，並將原則轉化為實踐。<br />\n2. 雖然指標資料凸顯了締約方在建立制度結構及落實取得與利益分享措施方面所取得的進展，但資料並未闡明這些制度與措施在達成議定書目標方面是否已投入運作或具備成效。令人擔憂的是，許多締約方仍有資訊尚未依據議定書第 14 條之要求，發布於取得與利益分享資訊交換所。<br />\n3. 人力資源與能力不足、國家聯絡點角色與責任之多樣性，以及不同主管機關或部會之間，或國家主管機關與檢查點之間內部協調之議題，仍是持續存在的挑戰。<br />\n4. 雖然與第 6 條實施相關的指標顯示締約方已取得顯著進展，但各國對於取得與利益分享之要求與程序的做法多樣化，對使用者而言構成了關鍵挑戰，包括在理解適用範圍與術語，以及在取得事先知情同意與許可證、協商共同商定條件及分享利益之步驟方面。此外，雖然國際公認的合規證明是提供取得之法律確定性及支持遺傳資源利用監測的重要工具，但迄今為止，僅有少數已落實取得措施的締約方在資訊交換所上發布了構成此類證明的許可證。<br />\n5. 制定清晰的程序（例如，為使用者提供適用規則與要求的逐步指南）、實用資訊及範本契約條款，並將其發布於資訊交換所，將使資訊交換所在達成其目標方面更具成效，即為使用者提供有關遺傳資源及其相關傳統知識之取得與利益分享的關鍵資訊。<br />\n6. 與第 5 條相關的指標顯示締約方已取得顯著進展，即便這些指標並未證明已落實的措施在達成議定書目標方面是否有效。應注意的是，締約方在回答報告相關問題時採取了不同的方法，部分締約方提供了關於確保在其管轄範圍內取得之遺傳資源或相關傳統知識利用之利益分享措施的資訊（透過事先知情同意與共同商定條件之要求），其他締約方則提供了關於確保從其他締約方取得之遺傳資源與相關傳統知識利用之利益分享措施的資訊（透過採取合規措施），還有其他締約方則同時處理這兩種方法。<br />\n7. 關於減少提供者（包括原住民族與地方社區）與遺傳資源使用者之間談判相關的不對稱性，有必要加強</p>","en":[4,5,6,7,8]}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2/p009.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3"},{"t":"the capacity of providers to negotiate mutually agreed terms and understand the commercial and non-commercial research environment, supply and value chains and the innovation process."},{"t":"8.     The assessment of the indicators measuring implementation of Article 15 indicated that significant progress has been made in establishing the foundational elements of the Protocol’s compliance provisions."},{"t":"9.     With respect to Article 17, the available information indicates that progress continues to be limited and uneven across regions and Parties.1 There are differences in understanding related to the role of checkpoints and significant challenges remain in fully operationalizing the provisions of the article, in particular with regard to the designation and operationalization of effective checkpoints by all Parties, as well as the use of checkpoint communiqués as part of the system for monitoring the utilization of genetic resources established under the Protocol."},{"t":"10. The situation described in paragraph 9 above is further illustrated by the limited number of checkpoints communiqués published which indicates that the monitoring system envisaged under Article 17 has not yet been widely or systematically implemented. A number of countries continue to be concerned about the misappropriation and misuse of their genetic resources once those resources leave their country which makes them more inclined to adopt access measures and systems for monitoring the utilization of their genetic resources that are more precautionary, as well as their own systems for monitoring utilization."},{"t":"11. Experience indicates that cooperation between user and provider countries remains important for enhancing compliance with domestic access and benefit-sharing measures. Much of the cooperation reported has been prompted by the issuance or receipt of checkpoint communiqués, underscoring the value of that tool for supporting compliance."},{"t":"12. Indicators related to the implementation of Articles 6, 7 and 12 show uneven progress. Among Parties that reported having indigenous peoples and local communities in their country, most included the requirement for prior informed consent in access and benefit-sharing measures and in that regard, indicators related to the Protocol’s provisions related to indigenous peoples and local communities showed moderate progress. However, many Parties have not yet fully operationalized those provisions and a limited number of examples have been reported, which highlights the need for case studies on practical experiences in implementing measures related to indigenous peoples and local communities."},{"t":"13. To improve the operationalization of the provisions related to indigenous peoples and local communities, it is essential to support the full and effective participation of indigenous peoples and local communities in access and benefit-sharing processes through early engagement, targeted awareness-raising and capacity-building, establishment of coordination mechanisms and empowerment."},{"t":"14. The development of community protocols is a critical first step, as it enables indigenous peoples and local communities to articulate their values, customary practices and aspirations and communicate them effectively to users of genetic resources and associated traditional knowledge and government authorities. In that regard, Parties need to further support the development and application of community protocols by indigenous peoples and local communities in accordance with Article 12 of the Protocol."},{"t":"15. There is a need to further strengthen political will to support the effective implementation of the provisions of the Protocol. That could be achieved through, for instance, highlighting the contribution of access and benefit-sharing to conservation and sustainable use of biodiversity; mainstreaming access and benefit-sharing in broader policy goals (as related, for example, to the"},{"t":"1 Forty-six per cent of Parties had established one or more checkpoints, with the following regional breakdown: 35 per cent of"},{"t":"Parties in Africa; 27 per cent of Parties in Asia-Pacific; 62 per cent of Parties in Eastern European States; 50 per cent of Parties in Latin America and the Caribbean; and 94 per cent of Parties in Western European and other States (see CBD/SBI/7/INF/2, para. 26 and figure 3)."},{"t":"9/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"提供者商定共同商定條件以及理解商業與非商業研究環境、供應與價值鏈及創新過程的能力。\n8. 衡量執行第 15 條之指標的評估顯示，在建立議定書遵約條款的基礎要素方面已取得重大進展。\n9. 就第 17 條而言，現有資訊顯示，各區域與締約方的進展仍持續受限且不均。$^{1}$ 有關檢查點角色之理解存在差異，且在使該條規定全面運作方面仍面臨重大挑戰，特別是關於所有締約方指定與運作有效檢查點，以及將檢查點通報作為議定書下建立之遺傳資源利用監測系統之一部分。\n10. 上述第 9 段所述之情況，可由發布的檢查點通報數量有限進一步說明，這顯示第 17 條所預期的監測系統尚未得到廣泛或系統性的實施。若干國家對於其遺傳資源一旦離開其國境後遭不當取得與誤用的問題持續表示關切，這使得其更傾向於採取更具預防性的取得措施與遺傳資源利用監測系統，以及其自身的利用監測系統。\n11. 經驗顯示，使用者國與提供國之間的合作對於強化國內取得與利益分享措施的遵約仍然重要。所報告的許多合作是由於檢查點通報的發布或收到所促成的，強調了該工具在支持遵約方面的價值。\n12. 與執行第 6、7 及 12 條相關的指標顯示進展不一。在報告其國家境內擁有原住民族與地方社區的締約方中，大多數在取得與利益分享措施中納入了事先知情同意的要求，在這方面，與議定書中關於原住民族與地方社區規定相關的指標顯示出適度進展。然而，許多締約方尚未完全運作這些規定，且報告的案例數量有限，這凸顯了對實施與原住民族與地方社區相關措施之實務經驗進行個案研究的需求。\n13. 為改善與原住民族與地方社區相關規定的運作，必須透過早期參與、有針對性的意識提升與能力建構、建立協調機制以及賦權，來支持原住民族與地方社區全面且有效地參與取得與利益分享程序。\n14. 社區議定書的制定是關鍵的第一步，因為它使原住民族與地方社區能夠闡明其價值觀、慣習做法與願景，並有效地將其傳達給遺傳資源及相關傳統知識的使用者以及政府主管機關。在這方面，締約方需要根據議定書第 12 條，進一步支持由原住民族與地方社區制定與應用社區議定書。\n15. 有必要進一步強化政治意願，以支持議定書規定的有效實施。例如，可以透過強調取得與利益分享對生物多樣性保育與永續利用的貢獻，以及將取得與利益分享主流化至更廣泛的政策目標中（例如，與","html":"<p>提供者商定共同商定條件以及理解商業與非商業研究環境、供應與價值鏈及創新過程的能力。<br />\n8. 衡量執行第 15 條之指標的評估顯示，在建立議定書遵約條款的基礎要素方面已取得重大進展。<br />\n9. 就第 17 條而言，現有資訊顯示，各區域與締約方的進展仍持續受限且不均。<sup>1</sup> 有關檢查點角色之理解存在差異，且在使該條規定全面運作方面仍面臨重大挑戰，特別是關於所有締約方指定與運作有效檢查點，以及將檢查點通報作為議定書下建立之遺傳資源利用監測系統之一部分。<br />\n10. 上述第 9 段所述之情況，可由發布的檢查點通報數量有限進一步說明，這顯示第 17 條所預期的監測系統尚未得到廣泛或系統性的實施。若干國家對於其遺傳資源一旦離開其國境後遭不當取得與誤用的問題持續表示關切，這使得其更傾向於採取更具預防性的取得措施與遺傳資源利用監測系統，以及其自身的利用監測系統。<br />\n11. 經驗顯示，使用者國與提供國之間的合作對於強化國內取得與利益分享措施的遵約仍然重要。所報告的許多合作是由於檢查點通報的發布或收到所促成的，強調了該工具在支持遵約方面的價值。<br />\n12. 與執行第 6、7 及 12 條相關的指標顯示進展不一。在報告其國家境內擁有原住民族與地方社區的締約方中，大多數在取得與利益分享措施中納入了事先知情同意的要求，在這方面，與議定書中關於原住民族與地方社區規定相關的指標顯示出適度進展。然而，許多締約方尚未完全運作這些規定，且報告的案例數量有限，這凸顯了對實施與原住民族與地方社區相關措施之實務經驗進行個案研究的需求。<br />\n13. 為改善與原住民族與地方社區相關規定的運作，必須透過早期參與、有針對性的意識提升與能力建構、建立協調機制以及賦權，來支持原住民族與地方社區全面且有效地參與取得與利益分享程序。<br />\n14. 社區議定書的制定是關鍵的第一步，因為它使原住民族與地方社區能夠闡明其價值觀、慣習做法與願景，並有效地將其傳達給遺傳資源及相關傳統知識的使用者以及政府主管機關。在這方面，締約方需要根據議定書第 12 條，進一步支持由原住民族與地方社區制定與應用社區議定書。<br />\n15. 有必要進一步強化政治意願，以支持議定書規定的有效實施。例如，可以透過強調取得與利益分享對生物多樣性保育與永續利用的貢獻，以及將取得與利益分享主流化至更廣泛的政策目標中（例如，與</p>","en":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[]},{"md":"$^{1}$ 46% 的締約方已建立一個或多個檢查點，其區域分布如下：非洲締約方為 35%；亞太地區締約方為 27%；東歐國家締約方為 62%；拉丁美洲與加勒比海地區締約方為 50%；以及西歐及其他國家締約方為 94%（參見 CBD/SBI/7/INF/2，第 26 段與圖 3）。","html":"<p><sup>1</sup> 46% 的締約方已建立一個或多個檢查點，其區域分布如下：非洲締約方為 35%；亞太地區締約方為 27%；東歐國家締約方為 62%；拉丁美洲與加勒比海地區締約方為 50%；以及西歐及其他國家締約方為 94%（參見 CBD/SBI/7/INF/2，第 26 段與圖 3）。</p>","en":[7,8,9,10,11]}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2/p010.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3"},{"t":"bioeconomy, research and innovation and development strategies) and showcasing the value of genetic resources and associated traditional knowledge. In that context, there is a need to change the narrative so that the third objective of the Convention is perceived not as a regulatory burden but rather as a strategic mechanism for valorizing biodiversity, supporting its conservation and sustainable use and creating opportunities for sustainable development."},{"t":"Element (g): review of implementation and operation of the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing- House, including number of access and benefit-sharing measures made available; number of countries that have published information on their competent national authorities; number of published internationally recognized certificates of compliance; and number of published checkpoint communiqués (Article 14)"},{"t":"G.1     National records on the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House","tb":1},{"t":"16. Overall, there has been a trend towards the continued increase in both the number of national records published across all record types and the percentage of Parties publishing national information. At the same time, however, the core objectives of the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House have not been completely met owing to the lack of full compliance by Parties with their obligations under Article 14 of the Protocol."},{"t":"17. Given the central role of the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House, it is of particular concern that, while many Parties have mandatory national information, they have not yet made it available on the Clearing-House despite having the capacity to publish that information, as illustrated by the high rate of submission of first national reports."},{"t":"18. The following reasons were given by Parties for not publishing information: insufficient resources, high staff turnover, lack of prioritization or coordination and lack of understanding of the Protocol’s system for monitoring utilization of genetic resources as elaborated under Article 17. Sharing of information through the Clearing-House has significant advantages for Parties, as it reduces queries from users about access and benefit-sharing, promotes compliance by users with domestic rules and procedures and supports Parties in monitoring the utilization of genetic resources internationally."},{"t":"Element (j): preliminary review of the compliance procedures and mechanisms (Article 30)"},{"t":"19. As experience related to the compliance procedures and mechanisms, including the Compliance Committee, is still relatively limited, it would be premature to make changes to them at this point in time. The compliance procedures and mechanisms are still being explored as a tool for supporting Parties in complying with their obligations under the Protocol. Increasing the visibility of the compliance procedures and mechanisms may be a useful means of encouraging Parties to engage with the Committee in its efforts to support compliance."},{"t":"10/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"生物經濟、研究、創新與發展策略相關）並展示遺傳資源及其相關傳統知識的價值，可透過上述方式來達成。在此脈絡下，有必要改變敘事方式，使公約的第三項目標不被視為監管負擔，而是一個用於提升生物多樣性價值、支持其保育與永續利用，並創造永續發展機會的策略機制。","html":"<p>生物經濟、研究、創新與發展策略相關）並展示遺傳資源及其相關傳統知識的價值，可透過上述方式來達成。在此脈絡下，有必要改變敘事方式，使公約的第三項目標不被視為監管負擔，而是一個用於提升生物多樣性價值、支持其保育與永續利用，並創造永續發展機會的策略機制。</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"要素 (g)：檢視取得與利益分享資訊交換所之執行與運作情況，包括已提供之取得與利益分享措施數量；已公布其國家主管機關資訊之國家數量；已公布之國際公認遵約證明書數量；以及已公布之檢查點公報數量（第 14 條）","html":"<p>要素 (g)：檢視取得與利益分享資訊交換所之執行與運作情況，包括已提供之取得與利益分享措施數量；已公布其國家主管機關資訊之國家數量；已公布之國際公認遵約證明書數量；以及已公布之檢查點公報數量（第 14 條）</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"G.1","html":"<p>G.1</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"取得與利益分享資訊交換所之國家紀錄","html":"<p>取得與利益分享資訊交換所之國家紀錄</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"16. 整體而言，所有紀錄類型的國家紀錄公布數量，以及公布國家資訊之締約方百分比，均呈現持續增加之趨勢。然而，同時由於締約方未能完全履行議定書第 14 條下之義務，導致取得與利益分享資訊交換所的核心目標尚未完全達成。","html":"<p>16. 整體而言，所有紀錄類型的國家紀錄公布數量，以及公布國家資訊之締約方百分比，均呈現持續增加之趨勢。然而，同時由於締約方未能完全履行議定書第 14 條下之義務，導致取得與利益分享資訊交換所的核心目標尚未完全達成。</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"17. 鑑於取得與利益分享資訊交換所的核心地位，特別令人關注的是，儘管許多締約方擁有強制性國家資訊，且具備公布該資訊之能力（如首份國家報告的高提交率所示），但尚未將其於資訊交換所上提供。","html":"<p>17. 鑑於取得與利益分享資訊交換所的核心地位，特別令人關注的是，儘管許多締約方擁有強制性國家資訊，且具備公布該資訊之能力（如首份國家報告的高提交率所示），但尚未將其於資訊交換所上提供。</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"18. 締約方提出不公布資訊之原因如下：資源不足、人員流動率高、缺乏優先順序或協調，以及缺乏對議定書第 17 條下詳述之遺傳資源利用監測系統之理解。透過資訊交換所分享資訊對締約方具有顯著優勢，因為這能減少使用者對於取得與利益分享的查詢、促進使用者對國內規則與程序的遵約，並支持締約方在國際上監測遺傳資源的利用情況。","html":"<p>18. 締約方提出不公布資訊之原因如下：資源不足、人員流動率高、缺乏優先順序或協調，以及缺乏對議定書第 17 條下詳述之遺傳資源利用監測系統之理解。透過資訊交換所分享資訊對締約方具有顯著優勢，因為這能減少使用者對於取得與利益分享的查詢、促進使用者對國內規則與程序的遵約，並支持締約方在國際上監測遺傳資源的利用情況。</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"要素 (j)：遵約程序與機制之初步檢視（第 30 條）","html":"<p>要素 (j)：遵約程序與機制之初步檢視（第 30 條）</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"19. 由於與遵約程序與機制（包括遵約委員會）相關之經驗仍相對有限，此時對其進行變更尚屬過早。遵約程序與機制仍正作為一項工具被探索中，用以支持締約方履行其於議定書下之義務。提高遵約程序與機制之能見度，可能是鼓勵締約方參與委員會支持遵約工作之有用手段。","html":"<p>19. 由於與遵約程序與機制（包括遵約委員會）相關之經驗仍相對有限，此時對其進行變更尚屬過早。遵約程序與機制仍正作為一項工具被探索中，用以支持締約方履行其於議定書下之義務。提高遵約程序與機制之能見度，可能是鼓勵締約方參與委員會支持遵約工作之有用手段。</p>","en":[8,9]}]},{"p":"p011","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2/p011.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3"},{"t":"Annex III"},{"t":"Indicative actions that could be taken at the national level to enhance the"},{"t":"implementation of the Nagoya Protocol"},{"t":"1.    Provided below is a list of indicative actions that could be taken at the national level, as appropriate and in accordance with national circumstances and priorities, to enhance the implementation of the Nagoya Protocol, based on experiences and lessons learned, and as a means to address identified challenges."},{"t":"Element (a): extent of implementation of the provisions of the Nagoya Protocol and related obligations of Parties, including assessment of progress by Parties in establishing institutional structures and access and benefit-sharing measures to implement the Protocol"},{"t":"2.     Establishing a clear policy vision prior to drafting legislation, as well as integrating and mainstreaming access and benefit-sharing into broader policy approaches (for example, with respect to the bioeconomy and research and innovation), can help build a solid framework and strengthen the political relevance of access and benefit-sharing."},{"t":"3.     Building flexibility in national access and benefit-sharing legal frameworks, for example, by adopting interim measures, can help Parties make adjustments as they gain experience. Over time, that experience could support further efforts to simplify procedures and standardize approaches for access and benefit-sharing."},{"t":"4.     Early engagement by the lead agency with other relevant agencies, clarity of roles and responsibilities, establishing effective coordination and communication channels among relevant authorities (such as committees or digital systems) and developing internal protocols and procedures can strengthen national coordination and cooperation. This would include national coordination and cooperation among entities responsible for access and benefit-sharing under different international instruments."},{"t":"5.    Establishing, where applicable, clear policies for full and effective participation of indigenous peoples and local communities and their inclusion in national committees on access and benefit-sharing would help ensure their ongoing engagement in access and benefit-sharing processes."},{"t":"6.     Early and ongoing engagement with users can help provider countries ensure that access and benefit-sharing procedures and measures take into account the perspectives and circumstances of users and support their compliance."},{"t":"7.     When national focal points and competent national authorities are being established, their mandates should fulfil the requirements under Article 13 of the Protocol and they should be equipped with adequate authority, dedicated personnel, capacity and training to be able to respond to users and indigenous peoples and local communities and negotiate mutually agreed terms. National focal points are also responsible for either taking on the role of publishing authority on the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House or designating another person for that role and are responsible for ensuring that all published information is accurate, complete and up to date."},{"t":"8.    Developing and promoting country guides, step-by-step procedures, standardized documentation including application forms, checklists summarizing needed information, template forms for mutually agreed terms, defined parameters for benefit-sharing, and a list of possible monetary and non-monetary benefits can greatly facilitate the access and benefit-sharing process. Availability (when possible) of information in different languages and provision of transparent national access and benefit-sharing requirements, including clear definitions of what falls within or is beyond the scope of national access and benefit-sharing measures, are key to helping users determine at an early stage whether access and benefit-sharing obligations apply and streamline preliminary exchanges."},{"t":"11/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"附件 III\n為強化名古屋議定書執行程度，可在國家層級採取之指標性行動\n1. 下列清單列出可在國家層級採取之指標性行動，視情況並根據國家情況與優先事項，基於經驗與教訓，並作為應對已識別挑戰之手段，以強化名古屋議定書之執行。\n要素 (a)：名古屋議定書規定之執行程度及締約方相關義務，包括締約方在建立制度結構及執行議定書之取得與利益分享措施方面之進度評估\n2. 在起草立法前建立明確的政策願景，以及將取得與利益分享整合並主流化至更廣泛的政策方法中（例如，關於生物經濟及研究與創新方面），有助於建立穩固的框架，並強化取得與利益分享的政治相關性。\n3. 在國家取得與利益分享法律框架中建立彈性，例如透過採取臨時措施，可幫助締約方在獲得經驗時進行調整。隨著時間推移，該經驗可支持進一步簡化程序及標準化取得與利益分享方法之努力。\n4. 主管機關與其他相關機關的早期參與、角色與責任的明確化、在相關主管機關之間建立有效的協調與溝通管道（例如委員會或數位系統），以及開發內部議定書與程序，皆可強化國家層級的協調與合作。這將包括在不同國際文書下負責取得與利益分享之實體之間的國家協調與合作。\n5. 在適用情況下，為原住民族與地方社區之充分且有效參與，及其納入國家取得與利益分享委員會，建立明確政策，將有助於確保其在取得與利益分享程序中的持續參與。\n6. 與使用者進行早期且持續的參與，可幫助提供國確保取得與利益分享程序與措施考量到使用者的觀點與情況，並支持其遵約。\n7. 在建立國家聯絡點與國家主管機關時，其職權應符合議定書第 13 條之要求，且應配備充足的權限、專責人員、能力與培訓，以便能夠回應使用者、原住民族與地方社區，並協商共同商定條件。國家聯絡點亦負責擔任取得與利益分享資訊交換所之發布機關角色，或指定另一人擔任該角色，並負責確保所有發布之資訊均為準確、完整且最新。\n8. 開發並推廣國家指南、逐步程序、標準化文件（包括申請表、彙整所需資訊之檢核表、共同商定條件之範本格式）、界定利益分享之參數，以及可能之金錢與非金錢利益清單，皆可大幅促進取得與利益分享程序。資訊（在可能情況下）以不同語言提供，以及提供透明的國家取得與利益分享要求（包括明確定義何者屬於或超出國家取得與利益分享措施之範圍），是幫助使用者在早期階段判定取得與利益分享義務是否適用，並簡化初步交流之關鍵。","html":"<p>附件 III<br />\n為強化名古屋議定書執行程度，可在國家層級採取之指標性行動<br />\n1. 下列清單列出可在國家層級採取之指標性行動，視情況並根據國家情況與優先事項，基於經驗與教訓，並作為應對已識別挑戰之手段，以強化名古屋議定書之執行。<br />\n要素 (a)：名古屋議定書規定之執行程度及締約方相關義務，包括締約方在建立制度結構及執行議定書之取得與利益分享措施方面之進度評估<br />\n2. 在起草立法前建立明確的政策願景，以及將取得與利益分享整合並主流化至更廣泛的政策方法中（例如，關於生物經濟及研究與創新方面），有助於建立穩固的框架，並強化取得與利益分享的政治相關性。<br />\n3. 在國家取得與利益分享法律框架中建立彈性，例如透過採取臨時措施，可幫助締約方在獲得經驗時進行調整。隨著時間推移，該經驗可支持進一步簡化程序及標準化取得與利益分享方法之努力。<br />\n4. 主管機關與其他相關機關的早期參與、角色與責任的明確化、在相關主管機關之間建立有效的協調與溝通管道（例如委員會或數位系統），以及開發內部議定書與程序，皆可強化國家層級的協調與合作。這將包括在不同國際文書下負責取得與利益分享之實體之間的國家協調與合作。<br />\n5. 在適用情況下，為原住民族與地方社區之充分且有效參與，及其納入國家取得與利益分享委員會，建立明確政策，將有助於確保其在取得與利益分享程序中的持續參與。<br />\n6. 與使用者進行早期且持續的參與，可幫助提供國確保取得與利益分享程序與措施考量到使用者的觀點與情況，並支持其遵約。<br />\n7. 在建立國家聯絡點與國家主管機關時，其職權應符合議定書第 13 條之要求，且應配備充足的權限、專責人員、能力與培訓，以便能夠回應使用者、原住民族與地方社區，並協商共同商定條件。國家聯絡點亦負責擔任取得與利益分享資訊交換所之發布機關角色，或指定另一人擔任該角色，並負責確保所有發布之資訊均為準確、完整且最新。<br />\n8. 開發並推廣國家指南、逐步程序、標準化文件（包括申請表、彙整所需資訊之檢核表、共同商定條件之範本格式）、界定利益分享之參數，以及可能之金錢與非金錢利益清單，皆可大幅促進取得與利益分享程序。資訊（在可能情況下）以不同語言提供，以及提供透明的國家取得與利益分享要求（包括明確定義何者屬於或超出國家取得與利益分享措施之範圍），是幫助使用者在早期階段判定取得與利益分享義務是否適用，並簡化初步交流之關鍵。</p>","en":[8,9,10,11,12]}]},{"p":"p012","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2/p012.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3"},{"t":"9.    Developing user support systems, including online systems for submitting and tracking access and benefit-sharing applications, and streamlined simplified approaches for permitting and negotiating mutually agreed terms can help reduce administrative burdens and transaction costs for providers and users."},{"t":"10. Engaging government departments with expertise in commercial business practices could provide support, for example, in the negotiation of mutually agreed terms and building the capacity of national institutions."},{"t":"11. Developing simplified procedures for non-commercial use to facilitate access can enable countries to maintain oversight while avoiding barriers to mutually beneficial scientific activities. Embedding access and benefit-sharing within broader institutional cooperation frameworks (for example, memorandums of understanding between research organizations, long-term research programmes and regional networks) could help build sustained collaboration and mutually beneficial outcomes."},{"t":"12. Establishing effective checkpoints and strengthening the institutional capacity to implement Articles 15 and 17 by all Parties will advance the full operationalization of the compliance and monitoring provisions of the Protocol."},{"t":"13. Enhancing awareness among users and providers, including Governments and indigenous peoples and local communities, and facilitating the exchange of information and experience on compliance measures can support compliance with access and benefit-sharing obligations."},{"t":"14. Supporting the full and effective participation of indigenous peoples and local communities in access and benefit-sharing processes is key for the implementation of the Protocol. This can be achieved through supporting the development and implementation of community protocols by indigenous peoples and local communities and raising their awareness and capacities as required by the Protocol. Those activities help empower communities to actively participate in access and benefit-sharing negotiations and build trust among all parties involved."},{"t":"15. Strengthening competent national authorities can play a role in identifying the relevant indigenous peoples and local communities to be involved and facilitate effective communication between users and representatives of indigenous peoples and local communities to strengthen coordination."},{"t":"16. Publishing community protocols on the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House as part of national records can give those documents greater visibility and recognition, as they would be included in a Party’s national access and benefit-sharing framework."},{"t":"Element (g): review of implementation and operation of the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing- House, including number of access and benefit-sharing measures made available; number of countries that have published information on their competent national authorities; number of published internationally recognized certificates of compliance; and number of published checkpoint communiqués (Article 14)"},{"t":"G.1     National records on the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House","tb":1},{"t":"17. Publishing all available national information on the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing- House and ensuring that it is accurate, reliable and up to date, in accordance with Article 14 of the Protocol, strengthens credibility at both the national and international levels; makes access and benefit-sharing requirements easier for researchers and companies to understand and follow; and enhances trust in the monitoring system established in the Protocol."},{"t":"18. Integrating training on the Clearing-House into onboarding activities can help address staff turnover. Resource materials are available on the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House knowledge base and online training and guidance, available from the Secretariat upon request, can assist Parties in building capacity and addressing any technical support issues related to publication of information on the Clearing-House."},{"t":"12/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"9. 開發使用者支援系統，包括用於提交與追蹤取得與利益分享申請的線上系統，以及簡化許可程序與協商共同商定條件的精簡方法，有助於減輕提供者與使用者的行政負擔與交易成本。\n10. 讓具備商業經營實務專業知識的政府部門參與，可提供支援，例如在共同商定條件的協商以及建立國家機構能力方面。\n11. 開發非商業用途的簡化程序以促進取得，能使各國在維持監督的同時，避免對互利之科學活動造成障礙。將取得與利益分享納入更廣泛的制度性合作框架（例如研究機構之間的合作備忘錄、長期研究計畫與區域網路），有助於建立持續性的合作與互利成果。\n12. 透過所有締約方建立有效的檢查點，並強化執行第 15 條與第 17 條的制度能力，將促進本議定書中遵約與監測條款的全面運作。\n13. 提升使用者與提供者（包括各國政府、原住民族與地方社區）的意識，並促進遵約措施之資訊與經驗交換，可支持遵守取得與利益分享義務。\n14. 支持原住民族與地方社區全面且有效地參與取得與利益分享程序，是執行本議定書的關鍵。這可以透過支持原住民族與地方社區開發與執行社區議定書，並根據本議定書之要求提高其意識與能力來達成。這些活動有助於賦權社區積極參與取得與利益分享的協商，並在所有相關方之間建立信任。\n15. 強化國家主管機關可在識別應參與之相關原住民族與地方社區方面發揮作用，並促進使用者與原住民族及地方社區代表之間的有效溝通，以加強協調。\n16. 將社區議定書作為國家紀錄的一部分，發布於取得與利益分享資訊交換所，可增加這些文件的能見度與認可度，因為它們將被納入締約方的國家取得與利益分享框架中。","html":"<p>9. 開發使用者支援系統，包括用於提交與追蹤取得與利益分享申請的線上系統，以及簡化許可程序與協商共同商定條件的精簡方法，有助於減輕提供者與使用者的行政負擔與交易成本。<br />\n10. 讓具備商業經營實務專業知識的政府部門參與，可提供支援，例如在共同商定條件的協商以及建立國家機構能力方面。<br />\n11. 開發非商業用途的簡化程序以促進取得，能使各國在維持監督的同時，避免對互利之科學活動造成障礙。將取得與利益分享納入更廣泛的制度性合作框架（例如研究機構之間的合作備忘錄、長期研究計畫與區域網路），有助於建立持續性的合作與互利成果。<br />\n12. 透過所有締約方建立有效的檢查點，並強化執行第 15 條與第 17 條的制度能力，將促進本議定書中遵約與監測條款的全面運作。<br />\n13. 提升使用者與提供者（包括各國政府、原住民族與地方社區）的意識，並促進遵約措施之資訊與經驗交換，可支持遵守取得與利益分享義務。<br />\n14. 支持原住民族與地方社區全面且有效地參與取得與利益分享程序，是執行本議定書的關鍵。這可以透過支持原住民族與地方社區開發與執行社區議定書，並根據本議定書之要求提高其意識與能力來達成。這些活動有助於賦權社區積極參與取得與利益分享的協商，並在所有相關方之間建立信任。<br />\n15. 強化國家主管機關可在識別應參與之相關原住民族與地方社區方面發揮作用，並促進使用者與原住民族及地方社區代表之間的有效溝通，以加強協調。<br />\n16. 將社區議定書作為國家紀錄的一部分，發布於取得與利益分享資訊交換所，可增加這些文件的能見度與認可度，因為它們將被納入締約方的國家取得與利益分享框架中。</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"要素 (g)：審查取得與利益分享資訊交換所之執行與運作情況，包括已提供的取得與利益分享措施數量；已發布國家主管機關資訊之國家數量；已發布之國際公認遵約證明書數量；以及已發布之檢查點公報數量（第 14 條）","html":"<p>要素 (g)：審查取得與利益分享資訊交換所之執行與運作情況，包括已提供的取得與利益分享措施數量；已發布國家主管機關資訊之國家數量；已發布之國際公認遵約證明書數量；以及已發布之檢查點公報數量（第 14 條）</p>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]},{"md":"G.1","html":"<p>G.1</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"取得與利益分享資訊交換所之國家紀錄","html":"<p>取得與利益分享資訊交換所之國家紀錄</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"17. 根據本議定書第 14 條，於取得與利益分享資訊交換所發布所有可取得之國家資訊，並確保其準確、可靠且最新，能強化國家與國際層級的公信力；使研究人員與公司更容易理解並遵循取得與利益分享之要求；並增進對本議定書所建立之監測系統的信任。\n18. 將關於資訊交換所的培訓整合至入職活動中，有助於應對人員流動問題。資源資料可於取得與利益分享資訊交換所的知識庫中取得，而線上培訓與指南（可根據要求向秘書處索取）可協助締約方進行能力建構，並解決與資訊交換所資訊發布相關的任何技術支援問題。","html":"<p>17. 根據本議定書第 14 條，於取得與利益分享資訊交換所發布所有可取得之國家資訊，並確保其準確、可靠且最新，能強化國家與國際層級的公信力；使研究人員與公司更容易理解並遵循取得與利益分享之要求；並增進對本議定書所建立之監測系統的信任。<br />\n18. 將關於資訊交換所的培訓整合至入職活動中，有助於應對人員流動問題。資源資料可於取得與利益分享資訊交換所的知識庫中取得，而線上培訓與指南（可根據要求向秘書處索取）可協助締約方進行能力建構，並解決與資訊交換所資訊發布相關的任何技術支援問題。</p>","en":[11,12,13]}]},{"p":"p013","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2/p013.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3"},{"t":"19. Developing national access and benefit-sharing information systems, including plans for their long-term sustainability, that are interoperable with the Clearing-House can help streamline the efficient publication of internationally recognized certificates of compliance and checkpoint communiqués and reduce the burden of manual publication."},{"t":"13/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"19. 建立與資訊交換所具備互通性的國家取得與利益分享資訊系統，包括其長期永續性計畫，有助於簡化國際認可之遵約證明書及檢查點公報的高效發布，並減輕人工發布之負擔。","html":"<p>19. 建立與資訊交換所具備互通性的國家取得與利益分享資訊系統，包括其長期永續性計畫，有助於簡化國際認可之遵約證明書及檢查點公報的高效發布，並減輕人工發布之負擔。</p>","en":[0,1,2]}]},{"p":"p014","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2/p014.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3"},{"t":"Annex IV"},{"t":"Actions that could be taken at the global or regional level to enhance the"},{"t":"implementation of the Nagoya Protocol"},{"t":"Element (a): extent of implementation of the provisions of the Nagoya Protocol and related obligations of Parties, including assessment of progress by Parties in establishing institutional structures and access and benefit-sharing measures to implement the Protocol"},{"t":"1.    Strengthening and supporting institutional capacity of Parties that still need such support to put access and benefit-sharing measures and institutional structures in place and operationalize them; and promoting a better understanding of access and benefit-sharing value chains and underlying market structures to inform policy- and decision-making."},{"t":"2.    Supporting Parties in the following priority areas: implementation of provisions related to indigenous peoples and local communities and Article 17; and publication of national information on the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House, as appropriate."},{"t":"3.     Facilitating the sharing of experiences and good practices among all actors to enrich the implementation of access and benefit-sharing measures, in particular in the priority areas. That includes encouraging exchanges between users and providers of genetic resources and associated traditional knowledge; and peer-to-peer support between Parties (such as support between national focal points and/or competent national authorities) at different levels of implementation or between provider and user countries. Those exchanges could be useful in supporting compliance."},{"t":"4.    Encouraging relevant regional organizations to actively engage in access and benefit-sharing processes. That could support the development of regional approaches to access and benefit-sharing."},{"t":"5.    Strengthening communication efforts with a view to changing the narrative so that the third objective of the Convention is perceived not as a regulatory burden but rather as a strategic mechanism for valorizing biodiversity, supporting its conservation and sustainable use and creating opportunities for sustainable development."},{"t":"6.  Promoting awareness of access and benefit-sharing among users in the scientific and business community across all countries."},{"t":"7.    Establishing and strengthening mechanisms to facilitate partnerships between users and providers of genetic resources and associated traditional knowledge, including by:"},{"t":"(a)    Developing matchmaking platforms or partnership hubs;"},{"t":"(b) Providing technical or legal advisory services for users and providers, including indigenous and people and local communities;"},{"t":"(c) Integrating access and benefit-sharing considerations into broader institutional cooperation frameworks such as memorandums of understanding between research organizations, long-term research programmes and regional networks, with mechanisms for facilitating technology transfer possibly included, where appropriate."},{"t":"Element (g): review of implementation and operation of the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing- House, including number of access and benefit-sharing measures made available; number of countries that have published information on their competent national authorities; number of published internationally recognized certificates of compliance; and number of published checkpoint communiqués (Article 14)"},{"t":"G.1 National records in the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House"},{"t":"8.    Strengthening the effectiveness of the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House to support the implementation of the Protocol through:"},{"t":"14/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"附件 IV\n可在全球或區域層級採取以強化《名古屋議定書》執行之行動\n要素 (a)：《名古屋議定書》條款之執行程度及締約方相關義務，包括締約方在建立制度結構及取得與利益分享措施以執行本議定書方面進展之評估\n1. 強化並支持仍需此類支持之締約方，以建立取得與利益分享措施及制度結構並使其運作；並促進對取得與利益分享價值鏈及底層市場結構之更好理解，以提供政策與決策參考。\n2. 在下列優先領域支持締約方：與原住民族與地方社區相關條款及第 17 條之執行；以及視情況於取得與利益分享資訊交換所發布國家資訊。\n3. 促進所有行為者之間經驗與良好實務之分享，以豐富取得與利益分享措施之執行，特別是在優先領域。這包括鼓勵遺傳資源及其相關傳統知識之使用者與提供者之間的交流；以及在不同執行層級或提供國與使用國之間，締約方之間（例如國家聯絡點及／或國家主管機關之間）的同儕支持。這些交流對於支持遵約可能具有用處。\n4. 鼓勵相關區域組織積極參與取得與利益分享程序。這可能有助於發展取得與利益分享之區域方法。\n5. 強化溝通工作，旨在改變論述，使公約第三項目標不被視為監管負擔，而是被視為一種提升生物多樣性價值、支持其保育與永續利用，並創造永續發展機會之策略機制。\n6. 提升所有國家科學與商業界使用者對取得與利益分享之意識。\n7. 建立並強化機制，以促進遺傳資源及其相關傳統知識之使用者與提供者之間的夥伴關係，包括透過：\n(a) 開發媒合平台或夥伴關係樞紐；\n(b) 為使用者與提供者（包括原住民族與地方社區）提供技術或法律諮詢服務；\n(c) 將取得與利益分享之考量納入更廣泛的制度合作框架中，例如研究機構之間的合作備忘錄、長期研究計畫及區域網路，且在適當情況下，可能包含促進技術轉移之機制。\n要素 (g)：審查取得與利益分享資訊交換所之執行與運作情況，包括已提供之取得與利益分享措施數量；已發布其國家主管機關資訊之國家數量；已發布之國際公認遵約證明書數量；以及已發布之檢查點公報（第 14 條）數量\nG.1 取得與利益分享資訊交換所中的國家紀錄\n8. 透過下列方式強化取得與利益分享資訊交換所之效能，以支持本議定書之執行：","html":"<p>附件 IV<br />\n可在全球或區域層級採取以強化《名古屋議定書》執行之行動<br />\n要素 (a)：《名古屋議定書》條款之執行程度及締約方相關義務，包括締約方在建立制度結構及取得與利益分享措施以執行本議定書方面進展之評估<br />\n1. 強化並支持仍需此類支持之締約方，以建立取得與利益分享措施及制度結構並使其運作；並促進對取得與利益分享價值鏈及底層市場結構之更好理解，以提供政策與決策參考。<br />\n2. 在下列優先領域支持締約方：與原住民族與地方社區相關條款及第 17 條之執行；以及視情況於取得與利益分享資訊交換所發布國家資訊。<br />\n3. 促進所有行為者之間經驗與良好實務之分享，以豐富取得與利益分享措施之執行，特別是在優先領域。這包括鼓勵遺傳資源及其相關傳統知識之使用者與提供者之間的交流；以及在不同執行層級或提供國與使用國之間，締約方之間（例如國家聯絡點及／或國家主管機關之間）的同儕支持。這些交流對於支持遵約可能具有用處。<br />\n4. 鼓勵相關區域組織積極參與取得與利益分享程序。這可能有助於發展取得與利益分享之區域方法。<br />\n5. 強化溝通工作，旨在改變論述，使公約第三項目標不被視為監管負擔，而是被視為一種提升生物多樣性價值、支持其保育與永續利用，並創造永續發展機會之策略機制。<br />\n6. 提升所有國家科學與商業界使用者對取得與利益分享之意識。<br />\n7. 建立並強化機制，以促進遺傳資源及其相關傳統知識之使用者與提供者之間的夥伴關係，包括透過：<br />\n(a) 開發媒合平台或夥伴關係樞紐；<br />\n(b) 為使用者與提供者（包括原住民族與地方社區）提供技術或法律諮詢服務；<br />\n(c) 將取得與利益分享之考量納入更廣泛的制度合作框架中，例如研究機構之間的合作備忘錄、長期研究計畫及區域網路，且在適當情況下，可能包含促進技術轉移之機制。<br />\n要素 (g)：審查取得與利益分享資訊交換所之執行與運作情況，包括已提供之取得與利益分享措施數量；已發布其國家主管機關資訊之國家數量；已發布之國際公認遵約證明書數量；以及已發布之檢查點公報（第 14 條）數量<br />\nG.1 取得與利益分享資訊交換所中的國家紀錄<br />\n8. 透過下列方式強化取得與利益分享資訊交換所之效能，以支持本議定書之執行：</p>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]}]},{"p":"p015","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6a32e728a192403aa236f5e2/p015.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/NP/CC/5/5-CBD/NP/MOP/6/3"},{"t":"(a) Enhancing the means by which relevant information for users is displayed on the Clearing-House to help them understand and comply with applicable access and benefit-sharing rules and procedures;"},{"t":"(b) Prioritizing improvements to Clearing-House functionality that support Parties in updating and publishing their national information and help ensure that the information is complete and reliable, for example, through automated reminders and streamlined record management processes;"},{"t":"(c) Providing proactive and targeted outreach and online training on how to use the Clearing-House, as needed, including for Parties with available national information not yet published on the Clearing-House;"},{"t":"(d) Sharing experiences and best practices in the development of national access and benefit-sharing information systems and promoting interoperability of those systems with the Clearing-House for efficient publication of national information, in particular internationally recognized certificates of compliance and checkpoint communiqués;"},{"t":"(e) Creating opportunities, incentives and recognition to encourage Party participation and demonstrate the value of the Clearing-House as a tool for supporting implementation of the Protocol;"},{"t":"(f)   Integrating the support for publication of relevant information on the Clearing-House into capacity-building initiatives supporting implementation of the Protocol;"},{"t":"(g) Strengthening capacity-building efforts related to the practical implementation of the Protocol’s international system for monitoring the utilization of genetic resources through the Clearing-House, which should include the role and function of internationally recognized certificates of compliance, checkpoints and checkpoint communiqués and opportunities to strengthen communication, cooperation and trust between provider and user country authorities."},{"t":"__________"},{"t":"15/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"(a) 加強資訊交換所在使用者相關資訊之呈現方式，以協助其理解並遵守適用的取得與利益分享規則及程序；\n(b) 優先改善資訊交換所之功能，以支持締約方更新並發布其國家資訊，並協助確保資訊之完整性與可靠性，例如透過自動化提醒與精簡的紀錄管理流程；\n(c) 根據需要，針對如何使用資訊交換所提供主動且具針對性的推廣與線上培訓，包括針對已有國家資訊但尚未發布於資訊交換所之締約方；\n(d) 分享開發國家取得與利益分享資訊系統之經驗與最佳實務，並促進該等系統與資訊交換所之間的互通性，以實現國家資訊之高效發布，特別是國際認可之遵約證明書與檢查點通報；\n(e) 創造機會、獎勵措施與認可，以鼓勵締約方參與，並展現資訊交換所作為支持議定書執行工具之價值；\n(f) 將支持於資訊交換所發布相關資訊之工作，納入支持議定書執行之能力建構計畫中；\n(g) 加強與透過資訊交換所實施議定書監測遺傳資源利用之國際系統相關之實務執行能力建構工作，其中應包括國際認可之遵約證明書、檢查點及檢查點通報的角色與功能，以及強化提供國與使用國主管機關之間溝通、合作與信任之機會。\n__________","html":"<p>(a) 加強資訊交換所在使用者相關資訊之呈現方式，以協助其理解並遵守適用的取得與利益分享規則及程序；<br />\n(b) 優先改善資訊交換所之功能，以支持締約方更新並發布其國家資訊，並協助確保資訊之完整性與可靠性，例如透過自動化提醒與精簡的紀錄管理流程；<br />\n(c) 根據需要，針對如何使用資訊交換所提供主動且具針對性的推廣與線上培訓，包括針對已有國家資訊但尚未發布於資訊交換所之締約方；<br />\n(d) 分享開發國家取得與利益分享資訊系統之經驗與最佳實務，並促進該等系統與資訊交換所之間的互通性，以實現國家資訊之高效發布，特別是國際認可之遵約證明書與檢查點通報；<br />\n(e) 創造機會、獎勵措施與認可，以鼓勵締約方參與，並展現資訊交換所作為支持議定書執行工具之價值；<br />\n(f) 將支持於資訊交換所發布相關資訊之工作，納入支持議定書執行之能力建構計畫中；<br />\n(g) 加強與透過資訊交換所實施議定書監測遺傳資源利用之國際系統相關之實務執行能力建構工作，其中應包括國際認可之遵約證明書、檢查點及檢查點通報的角色與功能，以及強化提供國與使用國主管機關之間溝通、合作與信任之機會。</p>\n<hr />","en":[3,4,5,6,7]}]}]};
